"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134672616,imgsize-749131.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[‘There’s so much money to be made’: Trump defends US data centres, warns they could go to China]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134672349.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/theres-so-much-money-to-be-made-trump-defends-us-data-centres-warns-they-could-go-to-china/articleshow/134672349.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/theres-so-much-money-to-be-made-trump-defends-us-data-centres-warns-they-could-go-to-china/articleshow/134672349.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-04T14:42:06+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aashish Vashistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134672488,imgsize-56432.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Antiques Roadshow Valuation: $100 Kleitsch find pegged at $500,000; painting later sells higher]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134655272.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A painting by Joseph Kleitsch that cost $100 in 1939 later gained a valuation of $500,000. The artwork depicts early Laguna Beach and showcases Kleitsch's significant contributions to California Impressionism. Following its appearance on Antiques Roadshow, the painting sold for an undisclosed amount exceeding the television valuation. It subsequently featured in exhibitions at the Irvine Museum and Laguna Art Museum in later years.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1939-a-california-family-bought-a-joseph-kleitsch-painting-from-his-widow-for-100-75-years-later-their-daughter-brought-it-to-antiques-roadshow-and-heard-a-500000-valuation/articleshow/134655272.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1939-a-california-family-bought-a-joseph-kleitsch-painting-from-his-widow-for-100-75-years-later-their-daughter-brought-it-to-antiques-roadshow-and-heard-a-500000-valuation/articleshow/134655272.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-04T16:58:33+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134655308,imgsize-1020459.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Leonardo DiCaprio gave $1 million to a Seychelles debt swap that protected 410,000 sq km of ocean]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134673582.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Seychelles protected 30% of its ocean by 2020 through a debt conversion deal linked to long-term conservation. The plan safeguards 410,000 sq km of ocean, while allowing sustainable fishing, tourism and other economic activities. Leonardo DiCaprio Foundation was among the private funders supporting the financial transaction.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/nature/leonardo-dicaprios-foundation-gave-1-million-to-a-seychelles-debt-swap-deal-by-2020-the-wider-project-had-helped-the-island-nation-protect-410000-sq-km-of-ocean-an-area-larger-than-germany/articleshow/134673582.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/nature/leonardo-dicaprios-foundation-gave-1-million-to-a-seychelles-debt-swap-deal-by-2020-the-wider-project-had-helped-the-island-nation-protect-410000-sq-km-of-ocean-an-area-larger-than-germany/articleshow/134673582.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-04T17:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134673818,imgsize-51782.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Astronomers spot gas falling onto a neutron star, revealing how matter reaches its surface]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134594156.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[On February 1, 2025, a research team used the XRISM telescope to study GX 301–2. They captured a unique event of gas falling onto a neutron star. The observations revealed changes in iron absorption lines from redshift to emission over time. The study suggests multi-phase accretion and indicates interactions with the stellar wind. These findings provide new insights into how neutron stars feed on surrounding matter.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/space/astronomers-spot-gas-falling-onto-a-neutron-star-for-the-first-time-revealing-how-matter-flows-towards-the-star/articleshow/134594156.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/space/astronomers-spot-gas-falling-onto-a-neutron-star-for-the-first-time-revealing-how-matter-flows-towards-the-star/articleshow/134594156.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-03T19:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134594251,imgsize-1337675.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Muskegon Lake had 347,350 tons of debris and 190,000 tons of contaminated soil removed]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134619771.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Muskegon Lake in Michigan has been officially delisted from the EPA's Areas of Concern list, marking a monumental milestone in restoration efforts. Over decades, key initiatives addressed challenges such as habitat degradation, pollution in soils, and shoreline hardening. With around $80 million dedicated to the cause, revitalized wetland habitats now support thriving fish and wildlife communities. This achievement heralds a brighter future for both the environment and local residents.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/after-40-years-as-one-of-the-great-lakes-most-degraded-sites-muskegon-lake-had-347350-tons-of-debris-and-190000-tons-of-contaminated-soil-removed/articleshow/134619771.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/after-40-years-as-one-of-the-great-lakes-most-degraded-sites-muskegon-lake-had-347350-tons-of-debris-and-190000-tons-of-contaminated-soil-removed/articleshow/134619771.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-03T16:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134620036,imgsize-171507.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[A 10.22-kg rock used as a Michigan barn doorstop was identified as a new iron meteorite]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134632686.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In 1939, a meteorite was unearthed on a Michigan farm and innocently pressed into service as a doorstop for many years. It wasn't until 2018, following the fall of another meteorite, that subsequent owners saw its true value. Central Michigan University performed an analysis and confirmed it as a new IIIAB iron meteorite, shedding light on the crucial role of personal specimens in advancing scientific knowledge.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/a-10-22-kg-rock-used-as-a-michigan-barn-doorstop-for-decades-was-identified-as-a-new-iron-meteorite/articleshow/134632686.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/a-10-22-kg-rock-used-as-a-michigan-barn-doorstop-for-decades-was-identified-as-a-new-iron-meteorite/articleshow/134632686.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-03T23:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134632783,imgsize-109162.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Meet Daniel Cox, the student behind a chemical-free weed control system]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134565780.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/meet-daniel-cox-a-sydney-student-who-built-a-solar-thermal-weed-control-system-that-achieved-92-weed-mortality-without-chemicals/articleshow/134565780.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/meet-daniel-cox-a-sydney-student-who-built-a-solar-thermal-weed-control-system-that-achieved-92-weed-mortality-without-chemicals/articleshow/134565780.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-03T14:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134566715,imgsize-225612.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Australia released 17 threatened bettongs into a predator-free reserve]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134567785.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Seventeen adult rufous bettongs were released into Ngambaa Nature Reserve after being translocated from Aussie Ark’s facility. This marks a significant step in reintroducing approximately 30 bettongs over the next 18 months. The nocturnal marsupials are essential for ecosystem health as they help disperse nutrients and fungi. They will be monitored using cameras and microchip scanners to track their progress.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/australia-released-17-threatened-bettongs-into-a-predator-free-reserve-the-digging-marsupials-could-help-restore-the-forest-ecosystem/articleshow/134567785.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/australia-released-17-threatened-bettongs-into-a-predator-free-reserve-the-digging-marsupials-could-help-restore-the-forest-ecosystem/articleshow/134567785.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-03T11:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134568262,imgsize-108863.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Military clothing fabric placed over strawberries produced 3.56 times more fruit]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134626594.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/a-fabric-developed-from-military-clothing-research-was-placed-over-strawberry-plants-field-tests-produced-3-56-times-more-fruit/articleshow/134626594.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/a-fabric-developed-from-military-clothing-research-was-placed-over-strawberry-plants-field-tests-produced-3-56-times-more-fruit/articleshow/134626594.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-03T10:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134632464,imgsize-154647.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Scientists turned waste wool into stiff building panels that helped reduce heat transfer]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134544686.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Researchers have found an innovative way to repurpose waste wool fibers into building panels. The panels, formed with keratin and citric acid, provide excellent insulation properties. Existing wool that is typically discarded can now be used in construction. This development addresses significant waste in the wool industry while promoting sustainability. The findings present an alternative to traditional building materials, enhancing eco-friendly construction practices.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/scientists-turned-waste-wool-into-building-panels-the-material-was-stiff-enough-for-cladding-and-helped-reduce-heat-transfer/articleshow/134544686.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/scientists-turned-waste-wool-into-building-panels-the-material-was-stiff-enough-for-cladding-and-helped-reduce-heat-transfer/articleshow/134544686.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-03T08:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134546786,imgsize-168378.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Coconut shell biochar makes asphalt stronger; 12.5% boosts heat resistance]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134545824.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/engineers-turn-coconut-shells-into-road-material-12-5-biochar-makes-asphalt-stronger-and-more-heat-resistant/articleshow/134545824.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/engineers-turn-coconut-shells-into-road-material-12-5-biochar-makes-asphalt-stronger-and-more-heat-resistant/articleshow/134545824